  2329	 IV. Conclusion
  2330	
  2331	       Like its parent the Smithsonian Institution, the Kennedy Center is an “odd federal bird.”
  2332	
  2333	Raven, 334 F. Supp. 3d at 29. It has both governmental and non-governmental qualities. That
  2334	
  2335	hybrid character leads to some likewise odd, and perhaps unintended, results. One such
  2336	
  2337	consequence is that the Center’s planned construction project—which is of substantial, though
  2338	
  2339	perhaps not entirely transformative, magnitude—does not plainly trigger the kinds of planning
  2340	
  2341	obligations it otherwise might. Another is that, because the Center does not qualify as an agency
  2342	
  2343	for APA purposes, DC Preservation League must overcome more exacting standards imposed by
  2344	
  2345	ultra vires and mandamus review. Those standards are not likely satisfied here, based on the
  2346	
