   143	I. Call to Order                                                                           Jennifer Fischer
   144	The annual meeting was called to order at 10:42 a.m. ET, held virtually via Zoom. A quorum of the Board
   145	of Trustees was confirmed to be present.
   146	
   147	II. Approval of Prior Meeting Minutes                                                      Jennifer Fischer
   148	A motion was called to approve the minutes of the June 11, 2026 Board of Trustees meeting.
   149	
   150	Representative Rick Larsen noted several typographical errors for staff to correct, and further noted that
   151	the formal name of the subcommittee that dealt with the reconciliation bill (referenced on p. 8) was
   152	stated improperly. Rep. Larsen advised that the correct formal name is the Subcommittee on Economic
   153	Development, Public Buildings, and Emergency Management, and that he would provide the correction
   154	to Mr. LaFauci. Vice Chair Fischer accepted the corrections.
   155	    Motion: by John Falconetti
   156	    Second: by Rick Larsen
   157	    Vote: Motion carried by show of hands, 25 in favor, none opposed, one abstention (Ms. Gross). The
   158	    minutes of the June 11, 2026 meeting were approved as amended.
   159	The minutes were further amended later in the meeting on the motion of Senator Whitehouse. See Item
   160	IV.
   161	
   162	III. Election of Officers                                                                       Joe LaFauci
   163	Mr. LaFauci advised the Board that, per the Bylaws, the annual meeting requires the election of officers,
   164	and that the Nominating and Governance Committee had met two days earlier, on Tuesday, August 11,
   165	2026, to consider the slate.
   166	
   167	General Counsel Elliot Berke observed that it would be recommended for the slate to be moved by a
   168	member of the Board who was not on the slate. Ms. Fischer confirmed that, as one of the officers, she
   169	could not bring the slate forward. Mr. Berke clarified that it is preferred to move the slate as a whole,
   170	rather than office by office.
   171	
   172	At the request of Representative Larsen, the slate was read in full:
   173	
   174	 Office                              Nominee
   175	 Chairman                            President Donald J. Trump          Re-election
   176	 Vice Chair                          Jennifer Fischer                   Re-election
   177	 Treasurer                           John Falconetti                    Re-election
   178	 General Counsel                     Elliot Berke                       Re-election
   179	 Secretary                           Brian Ballard                      New — succeeding Sergio Gor
   180	
   181	
   182	Representative Joyce Beatty asked whether there would be time for nominations from the floor, and
   183	whether other nominations had been submitted. Pamella Roland DeVos, chair of the Nominating and
   184	Governance Committee, responded that the Committee had largely carried forward the prior term's
   185	
   186	
   187	
   188	                                                                                                            3
