   384	disrepair. In thirty-six years, Mr. Buchalter has only seen one electrical room that looks like the
   385	electrical room at the Center. Once the utilities work is completed (cost $225M) , there would be
   386	insufficient funds (shortfall of $124M) to complete the structural renovation and no remaining funds at
   387	all for venue improvement. Revenues would be expected to decline, a compression Delta believes is
   388	already visible in year-over-year revenue decline because of uncertainty and friction; would expect that
   389	to continue. The main building does not segment well, gravitating around a core rather than separable
   390	wings; on a four-year assumption, approximately a third of the building would have to be closed at any
   391	given time, reducing programming space by a third (to allow for equipment etc). That’s additional
   392	revenue degredation. The capital program would be underfunded by as much as half, while the Center
   393	runs a meaningful operating deficit, directing fundraising toward the deficit and capital gaps rather than
   394	toward an endowment.
